page RecipeHandAnElementToAScript(path: "/recipes/hand-an-element-to-a-script", title: "Hand an element to a script — Recipes", description: "To give an element to a library and take it back when the element goes, use the three lifetime props.") {
    RecipeShell("Hand an element to a script", summary: "To give an element to a library and take it back when the element goes, use the three lifetime props. Every element and every component call takes them:  - `mount: (node) => …` runs each time the element is made: the first paint, a route change, an `if` branch arriving, a list item added. What it returns is the *handle* the other two receive. - `update: (handle) => …` runs again whenever the state it reads changes. - `cleanup: (handle) => …` runs when the element leaves (its page, its branch or its list item), so nothing a library made outlives it.  On a component call, the three belong to the component's root element, unless the component declares a prop of that name itself. A `mount:` that throws removes itself and logs the error; the page stays up.  To get a bare node for a library, use `Host`. It has the same lifetime: `Host(tag: \"canvas\", …)` makes the element the library wants. It makes a `div` by default, or a `span`, `canvas`, `svg`, `section`, `figure`, `pre`, `p`, `ul` or `table`.", outputs: [], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Call WF from a script", to: "/recipes/call-wf-from-a-script"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Call your own JavaScript", to: "/recipes/call-your-own-script"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Draw a chart from a library", to: "/recipes/chart-from-a-library")], source: "md-docs/recipes/hand-an-element-to-a-script.md", how: false, hasVariations: false) {
    }
}
